// The STUB declaration of the target configuration package.
//
// `target_cfg_pkg` describes the EXECUTION TARGET, not this device: can the
// runtime suspend a thread, does the image carry a solver. It is written by
// the tool or the environment, never by the model, and it has exactly one
// value per build. The full contract -- constants, provider obligations,
// defaults -- is `docs/target-cfg-contract.md`.
//
// This file declares the package and nothing else. Two reasons it exists:
//
//   * `compile has` needs a member path, and some front ends want the package
//     itself to resolve before they will answer a question about a member of
//     it. The LRM's own example (§19.3, Example275) declares the empty package
//     for exactly this reason. pssparser does not need it -- a `compile has`
//     naming an entirely undeclared package evaluates to false rather than
//     erroring -- but a stricter tool may.
//
//   * It documents, in the device tree, that this model has a target-config
//     dependency at all.
//
// A provider's declaration REOPENS this one rather than colliding with it:
// a package is a set of files (§18.1.1a). So this file stays in the build on
// every profile, configured or not.
package target_cfg_pkg { }
